From: bvchess <53128914+bvchess@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:05:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] Restricted problems of the frame model, for
 experiments: a board with holes, Y = 1..=n without some numbers (the holes
 theorem (X9)), and candidates barred or fixed at the root. Tables::with_holes
 takes the holes out of every list, so that the frames follow the
 maximal-factor rule of Y; setup takes the numbers above n/2 of the board as
 its sources, forms frames of its numbers only (a number up to n/2 that pays
 for no source is a frame alone, one layer above itself), gives an empty frame
 h to a layer of only closed frames between two with freedoms, and on a board
 with holes orders the frames by layer, since a chain of maximal factors from
 a move to a divisor can pass through holes. On the board 1..=n nothing
 changes. Prepared::restricted sets up the search of the node that promotes
 the fixed numbers, over the candidates less both sets, and refuses a number
 that is no candidate and the tactic symmetry. game::replay_with_holes
 referees moves on Y, and brute::solve_by searches it by either rule. The
 example restricted solves a restricted problem as an exact standalone search
 and checks the frame model's answers on small boards against brute force,
 X9's statement by a walk over the playable sets, U* made again by descending
 greedy, and the built-in table

